From 7362a553f13875f1b689108a59691ede9895c937 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zhangzhiqiang <zhangzhiqiang40@contributor>


Date: Mon, 21 Jul 2025 03:41:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH]     USERSTORY Multi join + distinct optimization

    Customer encounter performance regression for "LEFT JOIN + DISTINCT" scenario
    when they upgrade from RDS MySQL 5.7 to MySQL(for MySQL) 8.0.22 version.

    MySQL 8.0.16 introduce this performance regression issue when doing
    "Volcano iterator executor refactors", detailed commit as follows:
    [WL #12074: Volcano iterator executor base [9/15, temporary tables]]
    (https://github.com/mysql/mysql-server/commit/a56102e778ac63d50f53c5529922294019b8c254)

    This performance issue already been reported to community several years ago,
    and not been solved in latest release yet. Related bug info as follows:
    https://bugs.mysql.com/bug.php?id=109155
    https://bugs.mysql.com/bug.php?id=100536

    The reason for performance regression is old version(MySQL 5.7) distinct
    implementation, support pruning for all not_used_in_distinct tables. But
    new version(after MySQL 8.0.16) can only stop for the last not_used_in_distinct
    table when find out one new record(when JOIN::found_records updated).

    Refer to MySQL 5.7 Distinct implementatione, we stop traverse nested loop
    join inner table when find out a new record. In function
    "MaterializeIterator::MaterializeQueryBlock", update "join::found_records"
    if find one new record and "m_join" is not nullptr.
